{"line":20098,"timestampLocal":"2026-10-20T14:50:10","content":{"text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n**Effort and goal**\n- **Effort:** IMPL-UNITGREEN-001, finishing draft PR https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/87 (branch fix/unit-suite-green-20261019 into develop).\n- **Exit bar:** BDPv4 with 0 failed and 0 skipped on both lab hosts (Linux LAB-OMARCHY and Windows PAYTON-LEGION2), then a hostile AGREE at 98/98 from Codex gpt-6-astra max.\n- **Governing goal:** the operator's /goal (items 1 to 8, stop conditions, standing rules) still governs.\n\n**Earlier directions still in force (verbatim)**\n- \"Use the latest Roslyn tools!\"\n- \"I need you to get your goal completed without further scope creep.\"\n- \"Pause the C4 agent until your goal is complete.\" The C4 session asked to be notified when PR 87 merges after AGREE.\n- \"Looks like an opportunity to DRY\"\n- \"Please use ssh with the kingd key for execution on Legion2 so you have full access to the contents of the kingd home folder.\" This supersedes the goal's \"over WSMan\".\n- \"You have guidelines to make decisions within.\"\n\n**Operator AskUserQuestion answers this segment, in order**\n1. \"Fix scans in PR 87 (Recommended)\". Option text: BDPv4 bug fix in src so both scans skip links and IO errors; an AC on the owning TR, mock tree first; 19 marker tests made hermetic through the existing AgentPluginUserProfileOverride seam; 13 session-log tests tagged Integration; the PR closes triage b0e41c36.\n2. \"Fix the flake in PR 87 (Recommended)\". Option text: test-only; the three SQL Server classes share one default with a 120 s Connect Timeout; mock check first; all six gates rerun.\n3. \"Rerun for a complete set (Recommended)\". Option text: no code change, at most 2 more runs, checked by name against lane-2.\n4. \"Serialize SQL Server tests (Recommended)\". Option text: the four LocalDB classes join one xUnit collection; keep the 120 s connect timeout; they stay integration tests; mock check first; all six gates.\n5. \"Diagnose the loss in PR 87\". Option text: investigate why the Windows lane drops results and fix it here; unknown size; likely build or test-infrastructure changes and new criteria.\n\n**Operator heads-up this segment (pasted; requested a one-line confirmation, which was given)**\n- LAB-OMARCHY 10.42.0.214 keeps source at /home/sharpninja/github.\n- PAYTON-LEGION2 10.42.0.143 F:\\github is mounted at /mnt/legion2-github (fstab automount; \"If LEGION2 is off, the path is just unavailable; don't try to remount it\").\n- \"The link is a direct wire on 10.42.0.0/24. Use IP addresses, not hostnames.\"\n- Details are in Global memory MEMORY-PROCEDURE-001: \"Recall it through your plugin's memory tools, not raw REST.\"\n\n**Security and standing constraints (preserve verbatim)**\n- \"never read, print or copy /etc/samba/cred-legion2 or any password. Treat the other machine's tree as read-only unless I say otherwise, and never commit, push or run builds in it from here. Its McpServer is a separate store.\"\n- ~/.creds: \"Read and use, never print.\"\n- Never print or commit secrets or the marker API key.\n- MEMORY-INFRA-001: \"Never put passwords or private key contents in commands, logs, chat, memory or commits.\"\n- Never force-push.\n- No Python, no Node.\n- Bash only runs `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File <script.ps1>` with literal args. No -Command, no $, no backticks, no pipes. Quote globs. A value starting with '-' must use the colon form, for example -RemoteArgumentLine:-WhatIf.\n- Every script is analyzed with Invoke-Analyzer.ps1 and dry-run with -WhatIf before it runs.\n- Plugin routes only for the session log, TODO, requirements and triage.\n- No tables; no en or em dashes.\n- Sign commits \"Signed: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh@ClaudeCode | Confidence: ...\" followed by \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\". The PR body ends with \"🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\".\n- HV must not be run by the Claude family; the reviewer is Codex gpt-6-astra max.\n- Never move a file: copy, verify by hash, keep the original.\n- \"There should be ZERO platform specific UNIT tests. If it depends on the environment, it's an integration test.\"\n- No done state before AGREE.\n- Every text block opens with a stamp measured by /home/sharpninja/.claude/hooks/timestamp-guard/Get-LocalNow.ps1. Never estimate a stamp.\n- add-profile is the first action after every compaction or resume.\n- Do not read MEMORY-PROCESS-007 unless asked.\n- Present projected problems to the operator and get confirmation before launching HV.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n- **BDPv4 order:** requirement or AC first; then a test with scripted mock data and negative controls; then a green full Nuke Test mock gate; then the production change with the same assertions bound; then all gates.\n- **Gate set at the code head:**\n  - Linux Test (committed tree, before the push).\n  - Linux MigrationIntegrationTests lane.\n  - Windows Test over SSH as kingd.\n  - Windows interactive lane: a one-shot Interactive-logon task in kingd's session 1, runner SHA D04A018AFDDB198C0F113DC23EE86C7E059B3B3B1F9420F246EB10225A7002AE.\n  - Build.Tests (raw dotnet test, infrastructure).\n  - ValidateTraceability.\n  - D-A: later commits must be docs-only.\n- **Lane completeness:** a lane is complete only when compared by name with a complete run, because a lost result leaves total equal to executed in the TRX counters.\n- **Root cause of the lost Windows lane results:**\n  - xUnit v3 runs the test project as a separate process and sends JSON messages on its stdout (`-automated sync`).\n  - EphemeralPostgresFixture runs pg_ctl without output redirection, so pg_ctl's informational lines garble JSON lines.\n  - xUnit logs \"Received unparseable output from test process\", and a swallowed test-passed leaves RecordStart and RecordEnd with no RecordResult.\n  - Fix: pg_ctl -s.\n- **MSBuild properties from the environment:** `RunSettingsFilePath` maps to --settings and `VSTestDiag` to --diag (TestTaskUtils.cs). They are used only in the diagnosis runner.\n- **DirectoryTreeWalker:** breadth first; a directory link or reparse point is neither yielded nor descended; a directory whose listing throws IOException or UnauthorizedAccessException is yielded but not descended; file links are yielded; other errors propagate.\n- **xUnit v3 collections:** classes in one collection run sequentially, other collections stay parallel. `[assembly: AssemblyFixture]` with constructor injection.\n- **SSH:** `-o HostName=10.42.0.143 -o HostKeyAlias=PAYTON-LEGION2`, plus keepalives.\n- **Session id for this effort's turns:** ClaudeCode-20261019T134748Z-plugin-session. Hook turns go to failsafe, so I open explicit turns. PatchTurnAsync is additive.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n**Product code (commit 538d0ccf)**\n\n- **src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/DirectoryListingEntry.cs** (new):\n  `internal readonly record struct DirectoryListingEntry(string Path, bool IsDirectory, bool IsLink);` with TR-MCP-WS-005 / AC-TR-MCP-WS-005-001 and TR-MCP-SESSIONLOG-006 / AC-TR-MCP-SESSIONLOG-006-009 docs.\n- **src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/DirectoryTreeWalker.cs** (new): `internal sealed class DirectoryTreeWalker`.\n  - Constructor `internal DirectoryTreeWalker(Func<string, IReadOnlyList<DirectoryListingEntry>> list)`.\n  - `internal static DirectoryTreeWalker FileSystem { get; } = new(ListFileSystem)`.\n  - `EnumerateDirectories(root)` and `EnumerateFiles(root)` call `Walk(root, yieldDirectories)`: a breadth-first queue that skips directory links, enqueues and yields directories, and yields files.\n  - `TryList` catches IOException and UnauthorizedAccessException and returns `[]`.\n  - `ListFileSystem` uses `new DirectoryInfo(dir).EnumerateFileSystemInfos(\"*\", s_singleLevel)` with `EnumerationOptions { RecurseSubdirectories=false, IgnoreInaccessible=false, AttributesToSkip=0, ReturnSpecialDirectories=false }` and maps each entry to `(FullName, info is DirectoryInfo, (Attributes & ReparsePoint) != 0)`.\n- **src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/MarkerFileService.cs:**\n  - The three-argument `ResolveAgentPluginVersion` delegates to a new internal overload `(workspacePath, pluginName, environmentVariableName, string? userProfile, DirectoryTreeWalker walker)`.\n  - `EnumerateAgentPluginVersionRoots` and `EnumerateUserPluginCacheRoots` take the walker; `Directory.EnumerateDirectories(..., AllDirectories)` became `walker.EnumerateDirectories(...)`.\n- **src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/SessionLogTurnContextExtractor.cs:**\n  - Field `_walker`; an explicit public parameterless constructor `: this(DirectoryTreeWalker.FileSystem)`; `internal SessionLogTurnContextExtractor(DirectoryTreeWalker walker)`.\n  - CollectSources and AppendHistory take the walker; the try/catch around EnumerateFiles became `foreach (var file in walker.EnumerateFiles(root))`.\n\n**Tests (538d0ccf unless noted)**\n\n- **tests/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Tests/Services/DirectoryTreeWalkerTests.cs:**\n  - Seven scripted cases: nested-tree, untrusted-mount-point, access-denied, vanished-directory, directory-link, file-link, root-unlistable.\n  - `ScriptedDirectoryTree` (Lists, Throws, List, Listed; an unscripted directory throws InvalidOperationException) and an AssertWalk helper.\n  - Mock-gate tests: ScriptedCase_RequiredOutput_PassesTheWalkAssertion, ScriptedTheory_CoversEveryCase (7), ScriptedTree_RecordsListingsAndRefusesUnscriptedDirectories, WrongWalkNegativeControls_AreRejectedInsidePassingHarness and UnexpectedListingError_EscapesTheScriptedTree.\n  - Binding tests: ScriptedCase_ProductionWalk_YieldsTheRequiredOutput and ProductionWalk_UnexpectedListingError_Propagates.\n  - Integration test `[Trait(\"Category\",\"Integration\")]` FileSystemWalk_RealLinks_AreFlaggedAndNotDescended (real directory and file symlinks).\n- **tests/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Tests/Services/UserProfileScanBindingTests.cs:**\n  - Marker cases: ResolveAgentPluginVersion_UnlistableAndLinkedCacheDirectories_ResolveTheReachableVersion (expects 7.7.7, and 9.9.9 with the link flag removed) and ResolveAgentPluginVersion_CacheRootUnlistable_FallsBackToTheSyncedVersion.\n  - Extractor cases: Extract_UnlistableAndLinkedHistoryDirectories_ReadTheReachableHistory (PLAN-SCANBINDING-001, and None when the link is followed) and Extract_HistoryRootUnlistable_KeepsNone.\n- **tests/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Tests/HermeticUserProfileFixture.cs:** `[assembly: AssemblyFixture(typeof(HermeticUserProfileFixture))]`. Its constructor creates an empty temp profile and sets `MarkerFileService.AgentPluginUserProfileOverride`; Dispose clears the override only if it still holds this profile.\n- **tests/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Tests/HermeticUserProfileFixtureTests.cs** (race fixed in 56d14d7c):\n  - Injects the fixture through the constructor.\n  - AgentPluginUserProfileOverride_IsAnEmptyTemporaryProfile calls AssertHermetic on `_fixture.Profile`; the live override is only checked to be set and under the temp folder.\n  - HermeticityNegativeControls_AreRejectedInsidePassingHarness.\n- **MarkerFileServiceTests.cs:** WithHermeticPluginVersionResolution now saves and restores the previous override.\n- **12 import-path tests tagged Integration** (data file integration-traits-r3-import-path.psd1):\n  - SessionLogIngestorImportTests (5)\n  - FederatedSessionLogServiceTests.Apply_OmittedFields_PersistsProperValue\n  - SessionLogImportedSessionDeleteTests (3)\n  - SessionLogResubmissionReviveTests.SubmitAsync_ImportResubmitAfterTombstone_RevivesSession\n  - SessionLogServiceTurnContextTests.SubmitAsync_ImportMissingFields_ExtractsFromTurnText\n  - TranscriptSessionLogPersisterTests.Import_OmittedFields_PersistsExtractorResultOrNone\n\n**LocalDB connect timeout (6042dbb3)**\n\n- **tests/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Tests/Storage/SqlServerTestConnection.cs:** `internal static class`.\n  - `OverrideVariable = \"MCP_TEST_SQLSERVER_CONNECTION\"` and `ConnectTimeoutSeconds = 120`.\n  - `LocalDbDefault` is built with SqlConnectionStringBuilder: DataSource `(localdb)\\MSSQLLocalDB`, IntegratedSecurity, TrustServerCertificate, ConnectTimeout 120.\n  - `Server => Resolve(env)`; `Resolve(string? overrideValue) => overrideValue ?? LocalDbDefault`.\n- **SqlServerTestConnectionTests.cs:** AssertLocalDbDefault with 5 negative controls, plus the binding tests LocalDbDefault_PassesTheDefaultAssertion and Resolve_Override_IsReturnedUnchanged.\n- **Classes switched to `SqlServerTestConnection.Server`:** AuditPayloadProviderMigrationTests.cs (SqlServerAuditPayloadMigrationTests), SqlServerDecompose4nfBackfillMigrationTests.cs and SqlServerRenameQuadBrainRolesMigrationTests.cs.\n\n**SQL Server serialization (0210244d)**\n\n- **SqlServerLocalDbCollection.cs:** `[CollectionDefinition(Name)] public sealed class SqlServerLocalDbCollection { public const string Name = \"SQL Server LocalDB\"; }`. No DisableParallelization.\n- **`[Collection(SqlServerLocalDbCollection.Name)]`** on the four classes: SqlServerAuditPayloadMigrationTests, SqlServerDecompose4nfBackfillMigrationTests, SqlServerRenameQuadBrainRolesMigrationTests and SessionLogAgentSessionHeaderMigrationTests.\n- **SqlServerLocalDbCollectionTests.cs:** AssertInCollection reads CustomAttributeData; scripted nested types ScriptedMember, ScriptedOutsider and ScriptedOtherMember; binding test LocalDbClasses_AreInTheSqlServerLocalDbCollection.\n\n**pg_ctl silence (6ea425ab, the current code head)**\n\n- **EphemeralPostgresFixture.cs:** start uses `RunTool(..., PgCtlStartArguments(_dataDir, port, Path.Combine(_dataDir, \"pg.log\")))` and stop uses `PgCtlStopArguments(_dataDir)`. The new builders:\n  ```csharp\n  internal static string PgCtlStartArguments(string dataDir, int port, string logPath) =>\n      $\"start -D \\\"{dataDir}\\\" -w -s -o \\\"-p {port} -c listen_addresses=localhost\\\" -l \\\"{logPath}\\\"\";\n  internal static string PgCtlStopArguments(string dataDir) =>\n      $\"stop -D \\\"{dataDir}\\\" -m immediate -w -s\";\n  ```\n  An expanded comment explains the stdout and xUnit JSON reason.\n- **EphemeralPostgresFixtureArgumentsTests.cs:**\n  - AssertSilentWaitingCall uses the regexes `(^|\\s)-s(\\s|$)` and `(^|\\s)-w(\\s|$)` and checks that the string starts with the action.\n  - ScriptedSilentCalls_PassTheAssertion.\n  - LoudOrNonWaitingCalls_AreRejectedInsidePassingHarness (5 controls, including the old strings).\n  - Binding test FixtureCalls_AreSilentAndWait.\n\n**Scratch tooling (~/.claude/scratch/pr82-review-20261019/)**\n- **New scripts:** Find-ProfileLinks.ps1, Find-TrxTests.ps1, Get-CommitFileCounts.ps1, Push-Branch.ps1 (push only, with an expected-SHA check), Update-UnitGreenTodo-6.ps1 and Get-DevelopDelta.ps1.\n- **Remote scripts:**\n  - Test-WinSymbolicLinkCreation.ps1, Find-WinTrxTests.ps1, Wait-WinLaneExit.ps1, Compare-WinTrxRuns.ps1, Inspect-WinLaneLoss.ps1, Get-WinLocalDbState.ps1, Read-WinLaneDiagnostics.ps1, Read-WinVstestDiag.ps1, Read-WinLogRange.ps1, Get-WinUnparseableOutput.ps1 and Test-WinPgCtlSilent.ps1.\n  - Invoke-WinLaneDiagRunner.ps1 (diagnosis only, SHA A98190407B9EDC286619CDA3371550CD630A8B5E5A9872D858DE16C8C8B015BC). It writes a runsettings file with XmlWriter (xUnit DiagnosticMessages and InternalDiagnosticMessages, detailed console logger) and sets `$env:RunSettingsFilePath` and `$env:VSTestDiag`.\n- **Modified:**\n  - Start-WinInteractiveLane.ps1 gained `-RunnerName` (ValidateSet Invoke-WinLaneRunner.ps1 or Invoke-WinLaneDiagRunner.ps1).\n  - Get-WinTrxFailureStacks.ps1 gained `-Kind unit|provider`.\n  - Invoke-LegionSsh.ps1 now uses `$route = @('-o','HostName=10.42.0.143','-o','HostKeyAlias=PAYTON-LEGION2')` on every ssh and scp call.\n- **Unused:** remote/diag-lane.runsettings (left in place).\n- **Docs drafts** (scratch, not yet committed):\n  - plan-unit-s